ANTEATER POKER INSTALLATION
===========================

REQUIREMENTS
------------

- Linux
- GCC
- Make
- GTK+ 3
- Fontconfig

Building the graphical client from source requires the GTK+ 3 and Fontconfig
development packages.

INSTALLATION
------------

1. Extract the source archive and enter the project directory.
2. Compile the server and graphical client:

       make

3. Confirm that the executables were created:

       bin/poker_server
       bin/poker_client

RUNNING
-------

Start the server:

    make run-server

Then start a client in a separate terminal:

    make run-client

You may override the default network settings:

    make run-server PORT=10215
    make run-client HOST=localhost PORT=10215

PRECOMPILED CUSTOMER PACKAGE
----------------------------

The customer package already contains the compiled executables. Start the
server:

    ./bin/poker_server 10215

Then start each client in a separate terminal:

    ./bin/poker_client localhost 10215

Replace localhost with the server hostname when connecting from another
machine.

TESTING AND PACKAGING
---------------------

Run the communication smoke test:

    make test_comm

Launch each application for interactive testing with `make test_server` or
`make test_client`.

Create Poker_Beta_src.tar.gz:

    make tar

Create the customer package Poker_Beta.tar.gz:

    make customer_tar

UNINSTALLATION
--------------

Remove generated executables:

    make clean

Then remove the extracted project directory if it is no longer needed.
